<div class="tab {{tabs.battlefields.cssClass}}" data-group="primary" data-tab="battlefields">

{{! Its own tab rather than a panel inside Combat. A Battlefield is a thing the whole
    table is standing in rather than a number on one character, and the Combat tab is
    already a column of this character's own tracking values.

    Empty on purpose: the rules for this section have not been given yet. What goes here
    is written once they are, rather than guessed at from the name. }}
  <section class="panel">
    <h3 class="panel-title">Battlefields</h3>

    <p class="tab-placeholder">
      Nothing here yet. The Battlefields rules have not been built.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="panel">
    <h3 class="panel-title">What already points this way</h3>

    {{! Named rather than moved. The Weather row on the Combat tab is a fact about this
        character - what Battle Weathers count as for them - and it belongs there whatever
        Battlefields turns out to be. This is a pointer, so that whoever fills this tab in
        knows the Slot is already written and already read. }}
    <p class="tab-placeholder">
      Battle Weathers have a Slot (<code>weather.tiers</code>) and the Brace Maneuver
      writes it. There are no Battle Weathers in the library for it to be taken off, so
      the Combat tab states what it comes to and leaves the applying to the table.
    </p>
  </section>
</div>
